\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone 
\par 1. O God, my strength and fortitude,
\par In truth I will love Thee;
\par Thou art my castle and defence
\par In my necessity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone 
\par 2. When I, beset with pain and grief,
\par Prayed to my God for grace,
\par Forthwith my God heard my complaint
\par Out of His holy place.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone 
\par 3. The Lord descended from above,
\par And bow the heavens high,
\par And underneath His feet He cast
\par The darkness of the sky.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone 
\par 4. On cherub and on cherubim,
\par Full royally He rode;
\par And on the wings of all the winds
\par Came flying all abroad.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone 
\par 5. He brought me forth in open place,
\par That so I might be free;
\par And kept me safe, because He had
\par A favour unto me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone 
\par 6. Unspotted are the ways of God,
\par His word is truly tied;
\par He is a sure  defend to such
\par As in His ways abide.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\f2 
\par }

